From cd8cfe7ef2e9bf405c29dfc04a1afc4d1bcb60bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:46:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] SEO: key facts and FAQ on every listing page, with
 FAQPage JSON-LD

Every listing now shows, near the top and in the prerendered HTML, a Key facts
panel (who can apply, cost, dates) and an 'Info checked <month>' line, and
further down a short FAQ: when is the deadline / when do applications open,
is it free, who can apply. Answers come only from the listing's own fields;
anything the catalogue doesn't hold (amounts, essays, selectivity) points to
the official page. Dates never read just 'TBA': a passed deadline says so,
and a missing one names the cycle.

FAQPage JSON-LD mirrors exactly the FAQ the page shows (a test checks all
listings); listings with verified long-form copy keep their own FAQ.
EducationalOccupationalProgram and Article JSON-LD gain dateModified from the
listing's last real change. Single-grade programs no longer show '11-11'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015eydvdzcxBPZCXsPy7MGLS
